{"input": "Summarize the discussion about the working design of the remote control.", "answers": ["The industrial designer described the product as a portable device with some energy source, an interface which included some pressing buttons and keys, a processor, some infrared source which could send the information to the main device, and different encryption codes for different TVs. Since the Marketing and the user interface designer mentioned speech recognition, the industrial designer also took that into account. All these components would cost 5 Euros or even less than that. As for gesture recognition and automatic power control, the group gave them up due to price issues. At the end of the meeting, the group also talked about how to enable the users to find the controller."], "length": 7341, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The working design of the remote control includes a portable device with energy source, user interface with keypad and buttons, digital signal processor for processing user inputs, infrared LED for transmitting signals to the main device, and a switch in the main device for performing different operations based on the received signals. The design aims to provide simple actions for easy use and to be universal for different TV brands. The team discussed incorporating features like speech recognition, gesture recognition, and automatic on/off control, but decided to prioritize simplicity and cost-effectiveness."}
