{"input": "Summarize the discussion about the design of remote control for children.", "answers": ["The group thought remote controls should keep children safe while using them. At the same time, the remote control should be brightly coloured. Even if it is not colourful, it should also choose a monochrome colour that children like to attract them."], "length": 3236, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed the design of a remote control for children. They wanted it to be colorful, robust, and waterproof. It should have a simple and small design, with a limited number of buttons. The buttons should be easy to press and not prone to accidental presses. The remote control should be adaptable to both left- and right-handed users. It could have a color-changing frame and a screen that displays different colors depending on the user or the device it is controlling. The team also discussed the possibility of adding features like undo and history. They decided to work on the design and come up with a list of important and non-important features."}
