{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting", "answers": ["The meeting was about a computer based navigation system that will be used to conduct linguistic experiments on navigational terminology and intentionality, and it was simultaneously being recorded for another project. The navigational interface allows people to walk around a place and perform basic actions, like entering a building. Its goal is to understand what people intend to do based on granular linguistic features. The experimental set up is that people talk to a human assistant who controls the program in an attempt to complete a certain task. To study intentionality, the team will determine important linguistic features and use a Bayes model to see if they can predict the intention based on utterances."], "length": 15403, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the Meeting Recorder project, which aims to record and analyze real meetings. The participants discussed the importance of having a real meeting environment, using both far-field and close-talking microphones, and the need for a belief-net to combine contextual, linguistic, and discourse factors. They also talked about the proposed tasks, such as identifying the intentions of the speakers, and the need for a more sophisticated engine to extract features from the data. The meeting concluded with the plan to start collecting data and testing the belief-net."}
