{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The meeting was about caring Welsh children during the outbreak of COVID-19. Due to the coronavirus, the state was locked down and a strict social distance was required, and then most schools in Welsh were shut down. The group was concerned whether the existing support was enough to ensure their children get through such a period healthily, in terms of both mentally and physically. They listed several possible solutions, including having the vaccination on the susceptible group, offering psychological support for the children as well as the pregnant women, and raising a contingency fund. Through their asking and answering with the ministers, the group finally agreed on a bright blueprint for the education and economic recovery in Welsh."], "length": 10490, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting of the Children, Young People and Education Committee of the National Assembly for Wales was held on June 17, 2020. The committee met to discuss the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on children and young people in Wales. The Minister for Health and Social Services, Vaughan Gething, and the Deputy Minister for Health and Social Services, Julie Morgan, attended the meeting. The committee discussed various topics, including the impact of the pandemic on children's health and well-being, the availability of mental health services, the role of schools in supporting children's mental health, the provision of perinatal mental health services, the impact of the pandemic on vulnerable children, and the support provided by third sector organizations. The committee also discussed the Welsh Government's response to the pandemic, including the provision of funding for childcare services and the measures taken to protect vulnerable children. The meeting concluded with a discussion on the future of childcare services in Wales and the need for a support package for childcare providers."}
