{"input": "Summarize their discussions on pay dispute situations.", "answers": ["Dawn Bowden proposed the topic of pay dispute and asked what could be done as a Government to try to get parties back round the table and solve this dispute. Eluned Morgan thought this was about ColegauCymru's negotiation, and they were keeping a close eye on this situation. Eluned Morgan thought it would be fair to wait until they get further along down the line. Then Eluned Morgan had a detailed explanation about what they had done, including listening and speaking to ColegauCymru, and they were aware of what the unions were saying as well. Furthermore, Eluned Morgan said they would wish to see pay equality in relation to teaching, but details in relation to this should be waited until the outcome of the negotiations of ColegauCymru. They were aware of all those situations and they knew they were going to have to deal with it in the future."], "length": 13869, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The committee discussed the ongoing pay dispute between FE colleges and the Welsh Government. The Minister for Education, Kirsty Williams, stated that the Welsh Government is keeping a close eye on the situation and is in close contact with ColegauCymru, the representative body for FE colleges in Wales. The Minister acknowledged that the pay settlement for schoolteachers has been higher than that for FE teachers and expressed her support for pay equality between schoolteachers and FE teachers. The Minister also mentioned that the Welsh Government is aware of the potential impact of the upcoming pension changes on FE colleges and is prepared to take steps to mitigate the effects."}
