{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The meeting began with a discussion on the TORRENT project completion being pushed for two years. Grad F then introduced intermediate categorization, which was his topic for his qualification exams. The team then discussed mean subtraction from SRI. Using it had led to an improvement in Meeting Recorder digits though near mic performance worsened. The professor points to pre-echoes as the culprit. The team continued to study differences between SRI and Aurora. The team thought it would be interesting to do the Aurora tests with the SRI system instead of the HTK. The team was also exploring the Wiener filter and VTS. The professor did not seem too excited about the VTS."], "length": 11881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the progress of the Aurora system and the SRI system. The Aurora system has shown improvement in speech recognition accuracy, but the SRI system has not. The SRI system has a higher signal-to-noise ratio, but the improvement is not due to the mean subtraction. The SRI system uses more parameters and finer-grained acoustic models, which may be more sensitive to artifacts in the synthesized speech. The team plans to train the SRI system on a larger dataset to improve its robustness to artifacts. The meeting also discussed the reverberation time in the room and the possibility of using a high-pass filter to remove low-energy sections of the audio. The team plans to test the SRI system on the noisy TI digits and compare the results with the Aurora system."}
